{"abstract":[{"text":"Configure, combine, and morph views using Liquid Glass effects.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/technologies","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View-styles"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Applying-Liquid-Glass-to-custom-views"},"kind":"article","legalNotices":{"copyright":"Copyright &copy; 2026 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.","privacyPolicy":"https:\/\/www.apple.com\/privacy\/privacy-policy","termsOfUse":"https:\/\/www.apple.com\/legal\/internet-services\/terms\/site.html"},"metadata":{"availableLanguages":["de-DE","en-US","es-419","fr-FR","it-IT","ja-JP","ko-KR","pt-BR","zh-CN"],"modules":[{"name":"SwiftUI"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Applying Liquid Glass to custom views"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Interfaces across Apple platforms feature a new dynamic material called Liquid Glass, which combines the optical properties of glass with a sense of fluidity. Liquid Glass is a material that blurs content behind it, reflects color and light of surrounding content, and reacts to touch and pointer interactions in real time. Standard components in SwiftUI use Liquid Glass. Adopt Liquid Glass on custom components to move, combine, and morph them into one another with unique animations and transitions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"liquid-glass-landmarks-hero","metadata":{"deviceFrame":"iPadAir-13"},"type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To learn about Liquid Glass and more, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Apply-and-configure-Liquid-Glass-effects","level":2,"text":"Apply and configure Liquid Glass effects","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffect(_:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" modifier to add Liquid Glass effects to a view. By default, the modifier uses the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Glass\/regular","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" variant of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Glass","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and applies the given effect within a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Capsule","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" shape behind the view’s content.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Configure the effect to customize your components in a variety of ways:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use different shapes to have a consistent look and feel across custom components in your app. For example, use a rounded rectangle if you’re applying the effect to larger components that would look odd as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Capsule","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Circle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Assign a tint color to suggest prominence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Glass\/interactive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to custom components to make them react to touch and pointer interactions. This applies the same responsive and fluid reactions that ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/PrimitiveButtonStyle\/glass","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" provides to standard buttons.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the examples below, observe how to apply Liquid Glass effects to a view, use an alternate shape with a specific corner radius, and create a tinted view that responds to interactivity:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"identifier":"liquid-glass-view-examples","type":"video"},{"code":["Text(\"Hello, World!\")","    .font(.title)","    .padding()","    .glassEffect()","","Text(\"Hello, World!\")","    .font(.title)","    .padding()","    .glassEffect(in: .rect(cornerRadius: 16.0))","","Text(\"Hello, World!\")","    .font(.title)","    .padding()","    .glassEffect(.regular.tint(.orange).interactive())"],"copyToClipboard":true,"lineAnnotations":[],"showLineNumbers":false,"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","wrap":0},{"anchor":"Combine-multiple-views-with-Liquid-Glass-containers","level":2,"text":"Combine multiple views with Liquid Glass containers","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectContainer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" when applying Liquid Glass effects on multiple views to achieve the best rendering performance. A container also allows views with Liquid Glass effects to blend their shapes together and to morph in and out of each other during transitions. Inside a container, each view with the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffect(_:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" modifier renders with the effects behind it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Customize the spacing on the container to control how the Liquid Glass effects behind views interact with one another. The larger the spacing value on the container, the sooner the Liquid Glass effects behind views blend together and merge the shapes during a transition. A spacing value on the container that’s larger than the spacing of an interior ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/HStack","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/VStack","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", or other layout container causes Liquid Glass effects to blend together at rest because the views are too close to each other. Animating views in or out causes the shapes to morph apart or together as the space in the container changes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"glassEffect(_:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier captures the content to send to the container to render. Apply the ","type":"text"},{"code":"glassEffect(_:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier after other modifiers that affect the appearance of the view.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the example below, two images are placed close to each other and the Liquid Glass effects begin to blend their shapes together. This creates a fluid animation as components move around each other within a container:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"liquid-glass-joined-view","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["GlassEffectContainer(spacing: 40.0) {","    HStack(spacing: 40.0) {","        Image(systemName: \"scribble.variable\")","            .frame(width: 80.0, height: 80.0)","            .font(.system(size: 36))","            .glassEffect()","","        Image(systemName: \"eraser.fill\")","            .frame(width: 80.0, height: 80.0)","            .font(.system(size: 36))","            .glassEffect()","","            \/\/ An `offset` shows how Liquid Glass effects react to each other in a container.","            \/\/ Use animations and components appearing and disappearing to obtain effects that look purposeful.","            .offset(x: -40.0, y: 0.0)","    }","}"],"copyToClipboard":true,"lineAnnotations":[],"showLineNumbers":false,"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","wrap":0},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In some cases, you want the geometries of multiple views to contribute to a single Liquid Glass effect capsule, even when your content is at rest. Use the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffectUnion(id:namespace:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" modifier to specify that a view contributes to a unified effect with a particular ID. This combines all effects with a similar shape, Liquid Glass effect, and ID into a single shape with the applied Liquid Glass material. This is especially useful when creating views dynamically, or with views that live outside of a layout container, like an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"VStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"liquid-glass-unioned-views","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let symbolSet: [String] = [\"cloud.bolt.rain.fill\", \"sun.rain.fill\", \"moon.stars.fill\", \"moon.fill\"]","","GlassEffectContainer(spacing: 20.0) {","    HStack(spacing: 20.0) {","        ForEach(symbolSet.indices, id: \\.self) { item in","            Image(systemName: symbolSet[item])","                .frame(width: 80.0, height: 80.0)","                .font(.system(size: 36))","                .glassEffect()","                .glassEffectUnion(id: item < 2 ? \"1\" : \"2\", namespace: namespace)","        }","    }","}"],"copyToClipboard":true,"lineAnnotations":[],"showLineNumbers":false,"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","wrap":0},{"anchor":"Morph-Liquid-Glass-effects-during-transitions","level":2,"text":"Morph Liquid Glass effects during transitions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Morphing effects occur during transitions or animations between views with Liquid Glass effects. Coordinate transitions between views with effects in a container by using the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffectID(_:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" modifier. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectTransition","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" allows you to specify the type of transition to use when you want to add or remove effects within a container. For effects you want to add or remove that are positioned within the container’s assigned spacing, the default transition type is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectTransition\/matchedGeometry","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you prefer to have a simpler transition or to create a custom transition, use the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectTransition\/materialize","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" transition and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/withAnimation(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"materialize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" transition for effects you want to add or remove that are farther from each other than the container’s assigned spacing. To provide people with a consistent experience, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"matchedGeometry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"materialize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" transitions across your apps. The system applies more than opacity changes with the available transition types.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Associate each Liquid Glass effect with a unique identifier within a namespace that the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Namespace","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" property wrapper provides. These IDs ensure SwiftUI animates the same shapes correctly when a shape appears or disappears due to view hierarchy changes. SwiftUI uses the spacing provided to the effect container along with the geometry of the shapes themselves to determine when and which appropriate shapes to morph into and out of.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"glassEffectID(_:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"glassEffectTransition(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifiers only affect their content during view hierarchy transitions or animations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the example below, the eraser image transitions into and out of the pencil image when the ","type":"text"},{"code":"isExpanded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" variable changes. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"GlassEffectContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has a spacing value of ","type":"text"},{"code":"40.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"HStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" within it has a spacing of ","type":"text"},{"code":"40.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This morphs the eraser image into the pencil image when the eraser’s nearest edge is less than or equal to the container’s spacing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"identifier":"liquid-glass-morph-views","type":"video"},{"code":["@State private var isExpanded: Bool = false","@Namespace private var namespace","","var body: some View {","    GlassEffectContainer(spacing: 40.0) {","        HStack(spacing: 40.0) {","            Image(systemName: \"scribble.variable\")","                .frame(width: 80.0, height: 80.0)","                .font(.system(size: 36))","                .glassEffect()","                .glassEffectID(\"pencil\", in: namespace)","","            if isExpanded {","                Image(systemName: \"eraser.fill\")","                    .frame(width: 80.0, height: 80.0)","                    .font(.system(size: 36))","                    .glassEffect()","                    .glassEffectID(\"eraser\", in: namespace)","            }","        }","    }","","    Button(\"Toggle\") {","        withAnimation {","            isExpanded.toggle()","        }","    }","    .buttonStyle(.glass)","}"],"copyToClipboard":true,"lineAnnotations":[],"showLineNumbers":false,"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","wrap":0},{"anchor":"Optimize-performance-when-using-Liquid-Glass-effects","level":2,"text":"Optimize performance when using Liquid Glass effects","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Creating too many Liquid Glass effect containers and applying too many effects to views outside of containers can degrade performance. Limit the use of Liquid Glass effects onscreen at the same time. Additionally, optimize how your app spends rendering time as people use it. To learn how to improve the performance of your UI, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/videos\/play\/tech-talks\/10855\/","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/videos\/play\/wwdc2025\/306\/","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Styling-views-with-Liquid-Glass","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffect(_:in:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffectID(_:in:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffectTransition(_:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffectUnion(id:namespace:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Glass\/interactive(_:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectContainer","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectTransition","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassButtonStyle","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassProminentButtonStyle","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/DefaultGlassEffectShape"],"title":"Styling views with Liquid Glass"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftui\/applying-liquid-glass-to-custom-views"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-PageImage-card.png":{"alt":"An image with a background of Mount Fuji, and in the foreground screenshots of the landmark detail view for Mount Fuji in the Landmarks app, in an iPad and iPhone.","identifier":"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-PageImage-card.png","type":"image","variants":[{"traits":["2x","light"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-PageImage-card@2x.png"},{"traits":["2x","dark"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-PageImage-card~dark@2x.png"}]},"SwiftUI-PageImage-card.png":{"alt":"A stylized Swift logo using dashes on a white or blue background.","identifier":"SwiftUI-PageImage-card.png","type":"image","variants":[{"traits":["2x","light"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/SwiftUI-PageImage-card@2x.png"},{"traits":["2x","dark"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/SwiftUI-PageImage-card~dark@2x.png"}]},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI":{"abstract":[{"text":"Declare the user interface and behavior for your app on every platform.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI","images":[{"identifier":"SwiftUI-PageImage-card.png","type":"card"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"SwiftUI","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/Capsule":{"abstract":[{"text":"A capsule shape aligned inside the frame of the view containing it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Capsule"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Capsule","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Capsule"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Capsule","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/capsule"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/Circle":{"abstract":[{"text":"A circle centered on the frame of the view containing it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Circle"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Circle","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Circle"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Circle","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/circle"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/DefaultGlassEffectShape":{"abstract":[{"text":"The default shape applied by glass effects, a capsule.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DefaultGlassEffectShape"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/DefaultGlassEffectShape","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DefaultGlassEffectShape"}],"role":"symbol","title":"DefaultGlassEffectShape","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/defaultglasseffectshape"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/Glass":{"abstract":[{"text":"A structure that defines the configuration of the Liquid Glass material.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Glass"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Glass","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Glass"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Glass","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/glass"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/Glass/interactive(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns a copy of the structure configured to be interactive.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"interactive"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI5GlassV","text":"Glass"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Glass\/interactive(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"interactive(_:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/glass\/interactive(_:)"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/Glass/regular":{"abstract":[{"text":"The regular variant of the Liquid Glass material.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"regular"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI5GlassV","text":"Glass"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Glass\/regular","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"regular","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/glass\/regular"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/GlassButtonStyle":{"abstract":[{"text":"A button style that applies glass border artwork based on the button’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlassButtonStyle"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassButtonStyle","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlassButtonStyle"}],"role":"symbol","title":"GlassButtonStyle","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/glassbuttonstyle"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/GlassEffectContainer":{"abstract":[{"text":"A view that combines multiple Liquid Glass shapes into a single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shape that can morph individual shapes into one another.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlassEffectContainer"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectContainer","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlassEffectContainer"}],"role":"symbol","title":"GlassEffectContainer","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/glasseffectcontainer"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/GlassEffectTransition":{"abstract":[{"text":"A structure that describes changes to apply when a glass effect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is added or removed from the view hierarchy.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlassEffectTransition"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectTransition","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlassEffectTransition"}],"role":"symbol","title":"GlassEffectTransition","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/glasseffecttransition"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/GlassEffectTransition/matchedGeometry":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns the matched geometry glass effect transition.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"matchedGeometry"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI21GlassEffectTransitionV","text":"GlassEffectTransition"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectTransition\/matchedGeometry","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"matchedGeometry","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/glasseffecttransition\/matchedgeometry"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/GlassEffectTransition/materialize":{"abstract":[{"text":"The materialize glass effect transition which will fade in content","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and animate in or out the glass material but will not attempt to match","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the geometry of any other glass effects.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"materialize"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI21GlassEffectTransitionV","text":"GlassEffectTransition"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectTransition\/materialize","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"materialize","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftui\/glasseffecttransition\/materialize"},"doc://com.apple.SwiftUI/documentation/SwiftUI/GlassProminentButtonStyle":{"abstract":[{"text":"A button style that applies prominent glass border artwork based on the button’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlassProminentButtonStyle"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassProminentButtonStyle","kind":"